  = help: the trait `Expectation<{integer}>` is not implemented for `{integer}`
  = note: to compare with a plain value, wrap it in `eq(value)`. Other matchers are in `assertr::matchers`
  = help: the following other types implement trait `Expectation<T, R>`:
            `&D` implements `Expectation<T, R>`
            `AllOf<L>` implements `Expectation<A, R>`
            `AnyOf<L>` implements `Expectation<A, R>`
            `Anything` implements `Expectation<A, R>`
            `ContainsAll<E, B>` implements `Expectation<C, R>`
            `ContainsContiguous<E, B>` implements `Expectation<C, R>`
            `ContainsElement<B, E>` implements `Expectation<Range, R>`
            `ContainsEntry<'_, Q, E>` implements `Expectation<Mp, R>`
          and $N others
  = note: required for `assertr::__private::Cons<{integer}, assertr::__private::Nil>` to implement `MatcherList<{integer}>`
  = note: required for `ElementsAre<assertr::__private::Cons<{integer}, assertr::__private::Nil>>` to implement `Expectation<[{integer}; 1]>`
